{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:adffc4fc442f8f7b9e32af0f6c69a693e4ef1b9dec4708b61fb0738e64357681","title":"A finite inflationary episode provides an observable regulator of de Sitter space: modes leave the early Hubble horizon and can subsequently re-enter a decelerating universe. The relevant entropy changes with H and is evaluated at the end when bounding the total duration.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0000"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ad8d1c41689a7d10a99665fcc8c3f33d1d567da47103c3b1b229ca18a87ea518","title":"Can detectable inflationary tensors coexist with a string-derived microscopic description whose energy and field variables remain interpretable? The proposed example is an assisted multi-M5-brane system with an effective single canonical inflaton.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0003"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ade1654383f126e278cfd6836b5fa78793177147af3af75c41969138d083d75c","title":"Can high-scale inflation coexist with a present TeV-scale gravitino in large-volume compactifications, while avoiding destabilization and post-inflationary overshooting of the compactification minimum?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0005"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ade68997314b20e6fa12b920c3f53cca37dadcc9b6d6b8eab510c7dba0aff90d","title":"Can corrected Swiss-cheese compactifications support a nonsupersymmetric de Sitter minimum without anti-D3 uplift and axionic slow-roll inflation? Separately, how can extremal black-hole charges and fake superpotentials be obtained from prescribed attractor moduli?","connectionCount":3,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0006"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:adc0d95df7942e559e5152a47c04bb1b623e9f7a45bb73e7c854aadfb99836ed","title":"Can a family-universal Abelian gauge symmetry motivated by free-fermionic heterotic models protect the proton down to a low breaking scale while remaining anomaly free and allowing fermion masses and a neutrino seesaw?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0011"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ad7ca505da4b78e1e8cd9ec535b3fe24ddc438e91886b08e02eb5f5b792b42bf","title":"Can warping dynamically localise cosmic superstrings at a throat tip, including cosmological expansion and gravitational energy loss, or does internal motion persist sufficiently to affect gravitational-wave signals?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0012"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:adb1fb7322fa172aaa6544aaf924d33fed29b82bc6efc60a0e69772787974853","title":"Can long strings complete pure AdS3 gravity with boundary gravitons and a suitable BTZ mass gap, and can their classical collapse produce finite-energy states when string tension and back-reaction become large?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0017"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:adeb3be7531266f8c352feed040f87c499ced8e990c7f2888c57f3d4400afd32","title":"Under what conditions do anti-D3 uplifts in KKLT/KKLMMT and LVS admit a valid effective description of inflation and reheating, and when do one-loop corrections preserve classical soft-mass predictions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0022"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ad467f885fc12ef79ef45d7e2600fb4338d61a63e3ceb22ae9af5009f72d1236","title":"How do D-brane position and Wilson-line modes enter the flux-generated F-term potential together with closed-string moduli, and what do its discrete symmetries imply for holomorphic coordinates and the Kähler potential?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0022"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ada147e3d763277ce23584cb79825409ada4200825b2e7df029057248d44ec28","title":"Can an axionic inflaton traverse a parametrically large proper distance while spectator moduli remain stabilized and the hierarchy between inflation, moduli, Kaluza–Klein, string, and Planck scales preserves a four-dimensional effective description?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0024"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ade9bc25833aedd3c4d90eb12dbdefa7c05c1b8a61f211c4fd0fa1681f4a66a6","title":"Which classical backgrounds preserve every supercharge of a gauged or otherwise deformed supergravity, which gaugings admit pure AdS vacua, and which continuous scalar deformations preserve their supersymmetry? The holographic motivation is to constrain conformal manifolds of dual SCFTs.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0027"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:adcda1c497afc18070117fd5f67183ba403eb1bb5e899d14d8a29bec064ee607","title":"Can six-dimensional abelian gauge symmetries remain dynamical after gravity decouples, and how are the resulting abelian flavour symmetries characterized geometrically and on SCFT tensor branches?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0028"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ade1f05341da1573563bf55238b02db535886a493fe2ab63f9088c8dccfeafcb","title":"Which one-loop field redefinitions and Kähler potential simultaneously make the dilaton/untwisted Kähler-modulus kinetic terms compatible with N=1 supersymmetry and perturbative axionic shifts, and which string amplitudes fix their remaining coefficients?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0028"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ade71918e9da2c23020370c7a668029e2db0df2e0752da15f7bcf5eee43cad64","title":"After gauge constraints and contour choices are imposed, does a Euclidean axion wormhole have a physical negative mode, and would it imply decay by baby-universe emission? The reviewed calculations disagree.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0030"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:adb83ac3bccd28c2b053256ba8f51d7d22709d24e3d8cb8be9fa0907a755a68e","title":"Can massive type IIA supergravity admit four-dimensional de Sitter compactifications obtained directly from the full ten-dimensional equations with localized, backreacted orientifolds, and how far can weak coupling and small curvature justify their classical description?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0036"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:adc0a3074f6f8489a4a1270de75b2a78b3ba08e7feab41773a32cfd8360eed95","title":"The setting asks when quantum fluctuations can compete with classical inflaton motion while spacetime remains semiclassical. Higher-derivative interactions are represented through a sound speed, but the central curvature argument uses the unit-sound-speed limit.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0041"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ad5756f657d023274274a96f1749db5ce83fb8ae573f8fbed3545b82b723a3c9","title":"Can supergravity-motivated power-law potentials with exponential suppression yield observationally compatible inflation and sub-Planckian field excursions when embedded phenomenologically in braneworld cosmology?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0041"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ad053acb07e61d31fecd74582de9a84989a7d91983e9da027a8f8b27a419506b","title":"Can a small change in the power of the curvature-squared term alter Starobinsky inflation enough to reconcile its observable predictions with potential-based quantum-gravity conjectures?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0044"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ad98764bef83e0132a4bbeb9aa2401d0ac23fb2eef591614efb4f3c7afbdfbd6","title":"Which half-maximal three-dimensional gauged supergravities admit fully supersymmetric chiral N=(8,0) AdS3 vacua for n≤8 matter multiplets, and what are their embedding tensors, gauge groups, fluctuation spectra and possible embeddings into maximal supergravity?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0044"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ad9b51fdde2e9288e60750137f05715c9d28b2623f54302775ac60e6f03f928d","title":"Can thermomagnetic tachocline fields and axion–photon conversion explain solar magnetic cycles, luminosity variations and coronal heating, with asymmetric dark matter providing a clock connected to Galactic-center variability?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0044"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ad4cc1cb40a78ecf24bb3c2bd8eb4ee4af78f54932c3cbd9170eda91ae6b4e75","title":"How rapidly must a tower become light as geodesic field distance diverges?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0052"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ad3d22473312b5e18cad347b59aa11b8287ee5ab98f8ed90ee566fb78441a4a5","title":"The cosmological evolution is described through interacting vacuum and matter components, a canonical scalar representation, and an axion–condensate system. Comparing these descriptions requires separate field and energy-component dictionaries.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0056"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ad1c8f21341d44fa7c18b400b4ab3164100559853137e1c9bc4d3fe1bd214365","title":"Can five-dimensional quintessence catalyze metastable vacuum decay into a bubble carrying an expanding four-dimensional universe, and can catalytic selection plus the trans-Planckian censorship conjecture constrain its cosmological constant?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0059"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:adcf8cac73f0f831fe2c6d8f865fa6ece64bc2d263abe0fb49ab2b7d938e8145","title":"Can parity-violating CMB mode coupling measure an isotropic polarization rotation angle, and provide a competitive cross-check of the conventional EB power-spectrum measurement?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0065"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ad0fdac4e5e03791d68a361cc73b6be224d9441f033f091f95fa7760cd600809","title":"Which exceptional-curve intersection data must supplement an oriented bordism class to specify ADE singularities and associated gauge algebras?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0076"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:adf249b07b18434ba58b71fbc9873ff45a6694164faf5f0759e34b3b5fba5174","title":"Can the Dark Dimension proposal and the Gravitino Conjecture connect the observed dark energy density to supersymmetry breaking, and which tower configurations and string-inspired effective models support that connection?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0080"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:adf0169aa27472e7e4e28781d7dcb939e70e09f51700007bd08ab3ab22f30b5d","title":"How can cobordism-motivated end-of-the-world (ETW) boundaries mediate vacuum decay to nothing or creation from nothing, and how do defect size and tension determine semiclassical transition exponents?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0084"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ad265c44fc0fed7392c208fb2308bff9f8b87a958489cfc484df38ec4e52029f","title":"How do higher-derivative gravitational EFT operators change black-hole static tidal responses, when are Love numbers constant or running, and can charge enhance their observable effects?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0092"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ad9cd65130ccf5440e199a267f662b2457fec108b5d0ac7b0b572ebece0444c2","title":"Does the magnetic weak gravity conjecture–distance conjecture connection descend through Higgsing to a lower-energy EFT, and can excitations localized on its composite magnetic monopole supply the relevant tower?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0095"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ada8d151f5be8aea52454e10197f6455700bc9e49a025dd3fe4369fa6a1b9f71","title":"Can a dilaton running toward infinite bare coupling supply late-time quintessence, satisfy visible-matter gravity constraints, and sustain accelerated expansion with a finite dark-energy/dark-matter ratio?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0104"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ad5dc3b6424e5d800f8c6e587c2f9e8883a1a854fdc7ff97d02c789cea9f1b8b","title":"How can supersymmetric type II compactifications to four-dimensional Minkowski space be constructed on non-Calabi–Yau geometries, and how do NS/RR fluxes and geometric twists enter their supersymmetry constraints and effective superpotential? The paper also examines possible connections to smooth special-holonomy compactifications.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0109"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:adc83298ce056f932ebbcf7a463803b09bac81c152ad1fa01aa83c44eb4b061b","title":"Can exact classical heterotic backgrounds describe four-dimensional magnetic black-hole throats beyond the α′ expansion, and what do their small-charge limits imply for remnants and possible stringy resolution of gravitational singularities?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0118"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ad8911e6afad3818a92bed488fb81d81db6d0778029c89dd5a078d8b16c23c53","title":"What conformal-field-theory de